 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In nineteen eighty-three, a computer told one Soviet officer that American missiles were coming. He decided the computer was wrong.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 180
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "September twenty-sixth, just after midnight. A secret bunker outside Moscow.",
   "from": 183,
   "to": 309
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Lieutenant Colonel Stanislav Petrov is on watch. Weeks earlier, Soviet jets shot down a Korean airliner. Moscow fears an American first strike.",
   "from": 313,
   "to": 518
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then the siren. One American missile, launched. Then another. Then five.",
   "from": 522,
   "to": 624
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "officer",
   "text": "Comrade Petrov! What do we report?",
   "from": 628,
   "to": 686
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "His job: pass it up the chain. Moscow would have minutes to decide.",
   "from": 690,
   "to": 779
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, a real first strike wouldn't be five missiles. It would be hundreds.",
   "from": 782,
   "to": 896
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And ground radar had nothing to confirm yet.",
   "from": 899,
   "to": 958
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "petrov",
   "text": "False alarm. Report a system fault.",
   "from": 962,
   "to": 1019
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then he waits. Minutes pass.",
   "from": 1023,
   "to": 1074
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "officer",
   "text": "Still nothing, sir.",
   "from": 1077,
   "to": 1103
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The satellite had mistaken sunlight glinting off high clouds for rocket fire.",
   "from": 1107,
   "to": 1196
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Now, what if he'd reported an attack? His warning would have climbed to the Kremlin.",
   "from": 1211,
   "to": 1317
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Would they have fired? Some say other checks would have stopped it. Nobody wants to find out.",
   "from": 1321,
   "to": 1441
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "His reward? No medal back then. A reprimand, he said, over paperwork. The story stayed secret for fifteen years.",
   "from": 1444,
   "to": 1621
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Petrov later called it fifty-fifty. He bet the computer was wrong. And he was right.",
   "from": 1625,
   "to": 1736
  }
 ],
